 Assessment project was developed through the active involvement of stakeholders including residents and community groups in Oamaru.
An independent scientific analysis was undertaken to provide evidence to the local council to inform strategic decisions to make improvements to existing facilities or address emerging issues in a way that contributed positively to the local economy.
To achieve this goal, a team consisting of scientists from Auckland's Southern Cross Institute were engaged to undertake an analysis of transport in relation to local businesses in relation to walking routes around the Oamaru Business District.
With consideration of a range of outcomes including:
the health status of population;
employment rates within local industries and services;
proximity to local residential accommodation stock;
number of vehicles entering/leaving Oamaru CBDs every week.
Using statistical methods to predict expected levels of usage a ‘no improvement’ approach was taken where all variables either meet current needs or exceed them in the worst-case scenario (i.e. where traffic congestion is expected to exist).
